name=bitewrite
version=3.0
desc=A page where every letter lands like the launcher's — write, code that runs, lyrics that play, typing speed
category=visual
author=GLITCH-BITE-404
exec=run
deps=qml6:qt6-declarative python3:python py:numpy:python-numpy
usage=bitewrite   ·   opens a window · F1 write · F2 code · F3 lyrics · F4 speed · F5 settings
nopreview=bitewrite opens a window — there is nothing to sample into a text pane. Press Enter on it in INSTALLED to open the real thing.
keys=F1:WRITE — free writing, kept for next time|F2:CODE — write a program, or type one over its ghost|F3:LYRICS — type a song and it plays with you|F4:SPEED — a typing test, wpm live at the bottom|F5:settings — animations, sounds, everything, live|Ctrl+Enter:run what you wrote / play-pause the song|Tab / Shift+Tab:SPEED — change the time / the text|Ctrl+N:another snippet, song or text|Ctrl+R:start this one over|Ctrl+H:hide the ghost|Ctrl+S:save a copy to Documents|Ctrl+L:clear|Ctrl+= Ctrl+-:bigger / smaller|Ctrl+M:mute|Esc:back to WRITE, or close
about=The launcher's search box is the most satisfying thing in the shell to type into, and it only ever holds one short line. This is that box turned into a whole page, and then into four things to do with it. Every letter is its own animated object. By default it uses the launcher's exact pop (grows from a third of its size with the same OutBack overshoot, rises ten pixels, fades in over 140ms), and the settings swap that for drop, glitch, stamp, spin, float or random. Backspace can shrink letters away, drop them off the page, burst them into dust, flick them sideways or tear them apart. There are nine sound packs. launcher is the shell's own click at your sfx volume. The other eight are synthesised on first run: typewriter, thock, bubble, glitch, rain, and musicbox and chiptune, where every letter is a fixed note so your words come out as tunes. CODE runs whatever you wrote with Ctrl+Enter: broken code doesn't run and says so, valid code runs full-screen. You can start from a blank page (Enter indents after a brace, a closing brace steps back out) or type one of ten programs over its faint ghost and change it as you go. Long lines scroll the page sideways instead of running off the edge. LYRICS takes whatever is playing in Spotify, YouTube or mpv, or a file from your Music folder, finds its lyrics and makes them the ghost. In follow flow the song plays through the line you're on and waits at the start of the next one until you get there. Finishing a line and typing on drops you onto the next one. SPEED is a typing test. Pick 15, 30, 60 or 120 seconds, infinite, or a custom time, and random words, sentences, hard text or your own page. Your speed is live at the bottom the whole time, with accuracy, the clock and a sparkline. A timed run ends on a results card that keeps your best for each combination. Mistakes everywhere are counted word by word and line by line, so one slip costs one word, not everything after it. Every setting is in the F5 panel: it applies live while you type, the wheel scrolls it, Delete resets one setting, and a row at the bottom resets them all.
